O ce s of e stit te.- e following shallbe the O cers of the Insti e:(a) Patron;(b) Rector;(c) Pro-Rector;(d) Deans;(e) C irpersons;(D Regrs ier;ler of Examinations;(a) Director, Quality E ancement Cell;(i) irector, O ce of Research,I vation Commercialization;() Librarian; and(k) such o er persons as may be prescribed by Regulations to be the Officersof e Institute.
atro .- (l) The Patron or his nominee shall preside over a convocation of theInstitute.(2) The Institule may confer an honorary degree with the prior approval of the Patron.
I s ectio an iry. (1) The Patrpn may cause inspection or inquiry into theaffairs of the Institute.(2) The Patron shall convey his views with regard to the result of inspection or inquiryto the Board and may, after ascertaining the views of the Board, recommend anyremedial action to the oard.(3) The Board shall, wit n the time specified by the Patron, submit a report to thePatron about the action taken on the recommendations of the Patron.( ) If the Board fails to take action to the satisfaction of the Patron within the specifiedtime, the Patron may issue such directions as he thinks fit and the Board shall complywith all such directions.Provided that no action under subsection (4) shatl be taken unless the Chairman of theBoard is afforded an opportunity of being heard.
Rector. (1) The Board of Directors of the Company shall, on the recoinmendationsof the Board, appoint a person as Rector.(2) Board shall constitute a Search Committee for making reco endations forthe appointment of Rector.(3) The Board shall dete ine the terms and conditions of service of the Rector.(4) e Rector shall be the person who possesses the prescribed qualifications andexperience(5) The Rector shall perform such functions as are given in the Act or as may beprescribed or assigned to him by the Board.
Powers an duties o e Rector. (1) The Rector shall be the chief executive officerof the Institute responsible for all inistrative and academic functions ofthe Instituteand for ensuring that the provisions of the Act, Rules and Regulations are obsenred inall aftirs ofthe Institute.(2) The Rector may attend a meeting of any Authority or body of the Institute.
