egistr r. (1) The Board shall appoint a Registrar of the Institute.(2) The experience, professional and academic qualifications necessary forappointnent to the post of Registrar, method and manner of appointnent as well asterms and conditions of appointment shall be as may be piescribed by Regulations.(3) The Board shall not appoin! a person as Registrar unless he possesses theprescribed qualifications and experience and other reqdire:nents of the post.(a) The Registrar shall be a full-time officer of the Institute and shall:(a) be the administrative head of the secretariat of the Institute and beresponsible for the provision of secretarial support to the Board and theRector;(b). be the custodian of the common seal and the academic records of theInstitute;(c) maintain a register of the students and graduates in the prescribed manner;(d) prepare and update the Handbook of Rules and Regulations approved byA orities, bodies or committees from time to time, and make themavailable to public, all respective members of the Authorities and Offrcersof the Institute;(e) authenticate records on behalf of the Institute;(0 supervise the process of appointment or nomination of a member to anAuthority or body of the lnstitute in the prescribed manner; and(g) perform such other duties as may be prescribed or as may be assigned to(5) When the office of the Registrar is vacant or the Registrar is absent or unable tope rm his functions owing to any cause, the Board shall make temporaryarrangements for the performance of the duties of Registrar
