Board of over ors. (1) The Board of Govemors of the Institute shall consist of thefollowing:(a) A Director of the Company to be nominated by the Company shall be theChairman of the Board;' (b) Directors of the Co any subject to a maximum of four Directors to benominated by the Company;(c) Two persons from academia and industry each one of whom is an expert inany of the fields of knowledge to be nominated by the Chairrnan of theoard;(d) Secretary to the Gove ent, Federal Education Department or hisnominee;(e) Chairman of the Commission or his npminee;(D A Vice Chancellor of a Federal Institute of Pakistan to be nominated by thePatron;(g) Rector of the Institute;(h) Pro Rector of the Institute; and(i) Registrar (Secretary).(2) Members of the Board other than ex-fficio members shall hold offrce for a termof 'three years and shall be eligible for re appointnent on the exprry of their term ofoffice.(3) The 'quorum for a meeting of tfre Board shall be one-half of the total number ofmembers with at least two ex-fficio members, a fraction being counted as one.(a) The Secretary shall, wi the approval of the Chairman ofthe Board, call a meetingof the Board.(5) In the absence of Chairman ofthe Board, the Deputy Chairman ofthe Board shallpreside at the meetings of,the Board and perform all the functions and powers of theChairman.(6) The Board shall meet at least once in a calendar year.(7) Unless otherwise prescribed by this Act, all decisions of the Board shall be takenon the basis of the opinion of majority of the members present. In the event of themembers being evenly divided on any matter, the Chairman of the Board shall have acasting vote.(8) The Company may fill a casual vacancy occruring because of death or resignationof'a member of the Board nominated by the Company to the extent of the remainderof the term of the former member.
Fo drs' nd ies o the oard,- (1) The administration and management of theaJfairs of the Institute shall vest in the Board. The Board shall have the power ofgeneral supervision over the Institute and shall hold the Officers and authorities ofthe Institute accountable for all the functions of the Institute.(2) Without prejudice to the generality of the aforesaid power, the Board may:
